1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,410
This is VANA.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:07,974
In Hindi, VANA means forest. A quiet place to rest your mind,

3
00:00:07,974 --> 00:00:09,700
whenever you need it.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,340
Millions of people in India carry stress, anxiety and sadness in silence.

5
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:22,870
Therapy can feel expensive, far away, or simply hard to ask for.

6
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,857
And the heaviest moments often arrive at two in the morning,

7
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:28,690
when there is no one to talk to.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,560
VANA is a calm companion that listens, without judging.

9
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:38,179
Speak or type in English, Hindi, Marathi,

10
00:00:38,179 --> 00:00:40,425
or a mix of Hindi and English,

11
00:00:40,425 --> 00:00:42,970
and VANA replies in your language.

12
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,366
Soft forest sounds play in the background,

13
00:00:46,366 --> 00:00:50,160
so every conversation feels like a walk among the trees.

14
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:53,339
And if someone is in danger, VANA pauses,

15
00:00:53,339 --> 00:00:56,160
and points them to real people who can help.

16
00:00:57,902 --> 00:01:03,762
Let's see it. Asha creates her account, protected by her own password.

17
00:01:05,963 --> 00:01:10,253
She chooses a soundscape. Deep forest, today.

18
00:01:11,206 --> 00:01:13,466
Then she shares what's on her mind.

19
00:01:17,777 --> 00:01:21,997
VANA replies gently, with simple steps she can try tonight.

20
00:01:23,459 --> 00:01:26,814
The conversation is saved privately to her account,

21
00:01:26,814 --> 00:01:28,919
so she can return to it anytime.

22
00:01:33,473 --> 00:01:38,313
Asha can also write the way she speaks, mixing Hindi and English.

23
00:01:38,313 --> 00:01:42,483
VANA understands her, and replies in words she can read.

24
00:01:46,682 --> 00:01:48,862
Now, the most important part.

25
00:01:52,572 --> 00:01:57,627
When a message signals real danger, VANA does not improvise.

26
00:01:57,627 --> 00:02:00,492
It shows real, verified helplines.

27
00:02:01,104 --> 00:02:06,173
Tele-MANAS, one four four one six. Free, confidential,

28
00:02:06,173 --> 00:02:11,524
and open day and night. And one one two, in an emergency.

29
00:02:14,962 --> 00:02:20,472
Her privacy holds, too. With the wrong password, no one gets in.

30
00:02:24,128 --> 00:02:25,898
Under the hood, VANA is simple.

31
00:02:26,448 --> 00:02:30,728
A React app talks to a small Go service, hosted on Vercel.

32
00:02:31,278 --> 00:02:34,669
Every message passes a safety check first.

33
00:02:34,669 --> 00:02:37,415
Then a fast model on Groq replies,

34
00:02:37,415 --> 00:02:39,918
with Google Gemini as a backup.

35
00:02:40,468 --> 00:02:42,802
Conversations are stored in Supabase,

36
00:02:42,802 --> 00:02:45,388
linked only to the person who wrote them.

37
00:02:47,695 --> 00:02:49,675
VANA is built on four promises.

38
00:02:50,225 --> 00:02:54,937
Your password is never stored, only a secure fingerprint of it.

39
00:02:54,937 --> 00:02:57,555
Your conversations are yours alone.

40
00:02:58,105 --> 00:03:00,865
Crisis help is never left to chance.

41
00:03:00,865 --> 00:03:06,155
And VANA is here to support, but never to replace, professional care.

42
00:03:07,961 --> 00:03:10,831
VANA. A forest for the mind.

43
00:03:11,381 --> 00:03:14,331
Take a slow breath. We're listening.

